  "raw_text": "19\n\nMapara aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto contradict, to speak against\n \n/\n \ncontradecir, hablar en contra\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh20\n):\n \nBaibil selp ai mapara aisaras, sim lukanka atia brisa\n.\n \n–\n \nT\nhe Bible does not\n \nspeak against itself, all the thinking\n\nis the same (harmonious/not contradicting)\n.\n \n/\n \nLa Biblia no habla contra sí misma, todo el pensamiento es el mismo\n\n(armonioso/no contradictorio).\n)\n\nNina aisasara\n \n–\n \nslanderer, devil\n \n/\n \ncalumniador,\n \ndiablo\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n:\n \nslanderer\n \n/ calumniador\n \n–\n \nNina aisasara\n-\ndb\n,\n \nDahra kwakwahkra\n-\ndb\n,\n \nNina sasauhkra\n-\ndict,lv\n)\n\nParam aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak openly, to speak clearly\n \n/ hablar abiertamente, hablar claramente\n\nPura praki aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak in addition to, to exaggerate\n \n(\nhf\n)\n \n/ hablar además de, exagerar (\nhf\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nhf23\n):\n \nWahma bara tiara nani ba aima manis pura praki aisisa\n \n–\n \nYoung people often exaggerate\n \n/\n \nLos jóvenes\n\nsuelen exagerar\n)\n\nSturi aisaia\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nTuri aisaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto communicate, to\n \nconverse\n \n/\n \ncomunicar, conversar\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n07/19\n):\n \nUpla\n \nkum turi wan\n \naisisa taim, dîa muni\n \nt\nâ\nnka tara sa witin ra walaia bara rispik munaia?\n \n–\n \nWhen a\n\nperson communicates with us, why is it really important to listen and respect them?\n \n/\n \nCuando una persona se comunica\n\ncon nosotros,\n \n¿\npor qué es realmente importante escucharla y respetarla?\n)\n\nSturi aisanka tnatka\n \n–\n \nway\n \nor\n \nmanner of communicating, way\n \nor\n \nmanner of conversing\n \n/\n \nforma o manera\n\nde comunicarse, forma o manera de conversa\nr\n\nTnatka isi wal aisaia\n \n(\nth-17-tit\n)\n \n–\n \nUnderstandable to Others\n \n/ Hablar con Sencillez\n\nTnatkam ba kat aisas\n \n(\nth\n-\n2\n-\ntit\n)\n \n–\n \nConversational Manner\n \n/\n \nHablar con\n \nN\naturalidad\n\nUpla dîa bîla\n \nwin ba aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto quote a person, to say what a person said\n \n/\n \ncitar a una persona, decir lo que\n\ndijo una persona\n\nTâwan aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak up for, to speak for the sake of\n \n/ hablar por, hablar por el bien de\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nwqu-09/20\n):\n \nJisas nahki Meri t\nȃ\nwan aisan?\n \n–\n \nHow did Jesus speak up for (defend) Mary?\n \n/ ¿Cómo habló Jesús por\n(defendiendo) a María?)\n\nWitnis aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto witness, to testify, to bear witness\n \n/ testificar\n\nYukukras aisaia\n \n(\nbh21\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto speak without hiding, to speak honestly, to speak openly\n \n/ hablar sin esconder,\nhablar honestamente, hablar abiertamente\n\nAisawaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nAisauaia\n) (v-intrans)\n \n–\n \nto deteriorate, to rot, to ruin, to decay, to wear out\n \n/ deteriorarse, pudrirse,\narruinarse, descomponerse, desgastarse\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh184\n)\n \ndescribing worsening world conditions\n \n/ describiendo el empeoramiento de las condiciones mundiales\n:\n \ntasba saura\n\nna yu bani kau aisawi auya sa\n \n–\n \nthis bad world goes deteriorating more every day\n \n/\n \neste mundo malo se deteriora cada día\n \nmás\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\njl21\n)\n \ndiara nani aisawan ba kli paskisa\n \n–\n \nrestores\n \nthings that have deteriorated\n \n/\n \nrestaura cosas que se han deteriorado\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb-section5-intro\n)\n \nai kwalka aisawras kan\n \n–\n \ntheir clothes were not wearing out\n \n/ su ropa no se estaba desgastando)\n\nAisawan\n \n(v-3p-past/pasado, adj)\n \n–\n \ndeteriorated, rotten, ruined, decayed, worn out\n \n/ deteriorado, podrido,\narruinado, desgastado\n\nAiseya\n \n(\ndb,dba,bw,dbta\n)\n \n–\n \nIsaiah\n \n(Bible book) / Isaías (libro bíblico)\n\nAiska\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \ntotal, complete, entire, whole\n \n/ total, completo, entero\n\nAiskakira\n \n–\n \ntotal, complete, entire, whole, totally, completely, entirely\n \n/ total, completo, entero, totalmente,\ncompletamente, enteramente\n\nAiska pali\n \n(adv,adj)\n \n–\n \ntotally, completely, entirely, total, complete, entire\n \n/ totalmente, completamente, completo\n\nKupia aiska\n \n–\n \nwhole heart, whole-hearted, sincere\n \n/ todo el corazón, de todo corazón, sincero\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-10/19\n):\n \nJehova ra baman wan kupia aiska ni mayunpi\n \n–\n \nLet’s worship only Jehovah (exclusively) with our whole\n\nheart\n \n/ Adoremos solo a Jehová (exclusivamente) con todo nuestro corazón)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-10/20\n):\n \nWan kupia aiska trai munaia sa warkka wanki ba pain daukaia.\n \n–\n \nWe must try with our whole heart to\ndo any assignment we are given well.\n \n/ Debemos intentar con todo nuestro corazón hacer bien cualquier tarea que se nos\nasigne.)\n\nPiu aiska\n \n–\n \nfull-time, entire time\n \n/ tiempo completo\n\nPiu aiska smalki tataukra\n \n(\nkm\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspecial pioneer\n \n(of Jehovah’s Witnesses)\n \n/ precursor especial (de los\ntestigos de Jehová)\n\n(Note/Nota: Formerly/Anteriormente:\n \nPiu aiska smasmalkra\n \n(\njl13\n))\n\nAiskahkaia\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu-alt\n;\n \nAisakahkaia\n-\ndictu,dict-alt\n;\n \nAiskakaia\n-\ndictu-alt\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto become decorated, to become\nbeautiful, to become dressed, to become adorned, to decorate oneself, to beautify oneself, to dress oneself, to adorn\noneself\n \n/ decorarse, embellecerse, vestirse, adornarse, maquillarse, pintarrajearse\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nSkahkaia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-Param\n \nMarikan\n \n17:4\n):\n \nMairka na\n \n…\n \nwalpa manakira nani ni aiskahkan kan\n \n–\n \nThis woman was adorned with precious\nstones\n \n/ Esta mujer estaba adornada con piedras preciosas)",
